Collage, and co-produced by Will Smith.

12
01:08:52,173 --> 01:08:58,173
Smith stars as a runaway slave headed for Baton Rouge, Louisiana, in the 1860s, after President Abraham Lincoln issued the Emancipation
Proclamation to end slavery in secessionist Confederate states, surviving the swamps while being chased by slave catchers and their dogs.

13
01:14:36,521 --> 01:14:42,521
The film co-stars Ben Foster as a ruthless slave hunter and
Charmaine Bingwa as an enslaved wife and mother.

14
01:20:20,869 --> 01:20:26,869
The film is loosely based on the life of a self-emancipated
slave, known as either Gordon or "Whipped Peter".

15
01:26:05,217 --> 01:26:11,217
That story was made famous by the photograph of a man's bare back heavily scourged from an overseer's whippings, which was
published worldwide as a magazine illustration in 1863 and gave the abolitionist movement proof of the cruelty of slavery.

16
01:31:49,565 --> 01:31:55,565
Producer Joey McFarland began researching that story in
2018 and hired Collage to write the script.

17
01:37:33,913 --> 01:37:39,913
The film was officially announced in June 2020, with
Fuqua to direct and Smith to star.

18
01:43:18,260 --> 01:43:24,260
Filming was in Louisiana between July and August 2021, with Apple paying US$130 million
to acquire the rights to the film, outbidding several other studios.

19
01:49:02,608 --> 01:49:08,608
It was screened in Washington, D.C., on October 1, 2022, and released in select
cinemas on December 2, 2022, then streamed on December 9 on Apple TV+.

20
01:54:46,956 --> 01:54:52,956
The film received mixed reviews from critics, who praised Smith's performance but
criticized the screenplay and its handling of real-life events.

